{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":5,"timestamp":1777522212,"nonce":"sW/zTUL9FvoqDWPMdccxpZGAfiQ=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABA5fgj88AAAAF0zOMkA"},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"timestamp":1777522457,"nonce":"sK2tU5jcopfootFLr8rLIOHLnVg=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABA0I6hg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/111#issuecomment-4349639302"},"message":"Correction to the original issue body — both stacks **were** on RTK during the 2026-04-29 in-water session, contrary to the implication from `NavSatFix.status`.\n\nReading the right fields:\n\n| | source | RTK state | coverage |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| FCU (Cube Orange) | `/bizzy/mavros/gpsstatus/gps1/raw` (`GPSRAW.fix_type`) | RTK_FIXED (6) | **100.0%** (77724/77724, 28–36 sats) |\n| SBG Ellipse-D | `/bizzy/sensors/sbg/gps_pos.status.type` | RTK_INT (7) | **99.2%** |\n| | | RTK_FLOAT (6) | 0.4% |\n| | | SINGLE / PSRDIFF / INSUFFICIENT_OBS | \u003c1% combined |\n\nRTCM forwarding on `/bizzy/mavros/gps_rtk/send_rtcm`: 34761 msgs at 4.46 Hz over 7786 s, median inter-message gap 0 s, p95 1 s, max gap 8.5 s. Healthy.\n\nThe mavros `global_position/raw/fix.status.status` field stayed `0` (NavSatStatus.STATUS_FIX) throughout, which is misleading — mavros's NavSatFix translation does not lift `status` to `GBAS_FIX` even when the underlying FCU is reporting RTK_FIXED. Use `GPSRAW.fix_type` for FCU GPS truth, not `NavSatFix.status`.\n\n**Implication for this issue**: with both sources at cm-class RTK accuracy, the 0.635 m fore-aft body-frame offset and 0.024 m vertical residual are *real lever-arm geometry*, not GPS noise. That strengthens the case for projecting both streams to `base_link` rather than just letting the noise-floor hide the offset.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}